* on the nonseparating boundary, the pulled-back Hodge bundle has a trivial quotient, so \(\lambda_g=0\);
* on a separating boundary with genera \(h\) and \(g-h\), the Hodge bundle splits, and each term of \(\lambda_g\lambda_{g-1}\) contains either \(\lambda_h^2\) or \(\lambda_{g-h}^2\), both zero by Mumford’s relation.

Consequently, localization makes
\[
\alpha\longmapsto
\int_{\overline{\mathcal M}_{25}}\widetilde\alpha\,\lambda_{25}\lambda_{24}
