This code uses only the Python standard library. It constructs the relations and the intersection matrix from the formulas above; it does not insert their ranks as data.

In `kap`, the factor \((|c|-1)!\) counts cycles on a chosen set of labels. Zero indices are removed using
\[
\mathsf K(K_0^zK_{e_1}\cdots K_{e_m})
=(48+m)(49+m)\cdots(47+m+z)\,
